<meta>
  title: Quotarelay
  description: MCP-first context compression for coding agents, with a free Apache-2.0 local tool and planned paid team coordination.
  keywords: quotarelay, mcp, coding agents, context compression, local first, token savings
  aiSummary: Quotarelay is an MCP-first agent tool that assembles bounded, explainable context packets for coding agents while keeping repository contents local by default.
  aiKeywords: mcp, context-engine, local-first, coding-agents, privacy, open-core
</meta>

<route>
  path: /
</route>

<ai>
  summary: Public product homepage for Quotarelay. Present Quotarelay as an MCP-first agent tool, not a desktop or mobile app, and clearly distinguish planned hosted team features.
  audience:
    - solo developers
    - engineering teams
    - AI coding tool users
  privacy_boundary: Source code, raw context packets, local caches, and .quotarelay state stay local by default.
  monetization: Free Apache-2.0 local core with paid hosted/team/enterprise coordination planned.
  tags:
    - public-site
    - local-first
    - mcp
    - context-compression
    - privacy
</ai>

<script>
  import { deploymentSurfaces, surfaceStatusLabel } from '../deploymentSurfaces'

  function surfaces() {
    return deploymentSurfaces
  }

  function statusLabel(status) {
    return surfaceStatusLabel(status)
  }
</script>

<template>
  <main class="public-site">
    <section class="public-hero">
      <div class="public-hero__copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">MCP-first agent tool</p>
        <h1>Quotarelay</h1>
        <p class="public-lede">
          Connect Quotarelay to your coding agent so it sends less repo context. The local MCP tool returns relevant
          code, durable decisions, validation commands, cache state, stale-state warnings, and omission reasons without
          uploading your repository by default.
        </p>
        <div class="public-actions">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="https://github.com/quotarelay/quotarelay">GitHub</a>
          <a class="button button--secondary" href="/control-plane">Local control plane</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="signal-board" aria-label="Quotarelay packet proof summary">
        <div class="signal-board__header">
          <span>Context packet</span>
          <strong>bounded</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="signal-row">
          <span>Raw bytes considered</span>
          <strong>24,106</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="signal-row">
          <span>Packet bytes</span>
          <strong>1,361</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="signal-row">
          <span>Local reduction</span>
          <strong>94.35%</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="signal-row signal-row--accent">
          <span>Repeat retrieval</span>
          <strong>cache hit</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-band">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">What ships free</p>
        <h2>A useful local MCP tool, not a native app detour.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature-card">
          <h3>Agent connection</h3>
          <p>Run from source with Cargo or install the local `quotarelay-mcp` command for stdio MCP clients.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
          <h3>Bounded retrieval</h3>
          <p>Exact, overview, task, and diff-aware modes return limited context with typed inclusion and omission reasons.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
          <h3>Memory and handoff</h3>
          <p>Local decision and guardrail memory can travel with handoff packets, validation suggestions, and blockers.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
          <h3>Savings proof</h3>
          <p>Local demos report raw bytes, packet bytes, approximate tokens, reduction ratio, cache state, and stale state.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
          <h3>Privacy boundary</h3>
          <p>Repository contents, raw packets, local caches, and .quotarelay state stay on your machine unless you opt in later.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="public-band public-band--split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Teams and companies</p>
        <h2>Paid value belongs in coordination, governance, and support.</h2>
        <p class="public-copy">
          Quotarelay should be easy to adopt as an open-source local tool. The commercial layer is planned around
          hosted team management, shared policy profiles, aggregate savings reports, auditability, integrations,
          private deployment guidance, SSO, onboarding, and support. Desktop and mobile apps are deferred until
          users prove a companion wrapper is more useful than direct agent integration.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="team-list">
        <li>Organization login and team membership</li>
        <li>Shared guardrails and validation recipes</li>
        <li>Aggregate savings and cache-reuse reporting</li>
        <li>Audit logs, SSO, compliance docs, and private deployment</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="public-band">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Platform surfaces</p>
        <h2>One workspace, separate targets.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="surface-grid">
        <article class="surface-card" v-for="surface in surfaces()" :key="surface.id">
          <div class="surface-card__header">
            <span class="surface-status">{{ statusLabel(surface.status) }}</span>
            <strong>{{ surface.target }}</strong>
          </div>
          <h3>{{ surface.title }}</h3>
          <p>{{ surface.localPreview }}</p>
          <p class="surface-boundary">{{ surface.deploymentBoundary }}</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</template>
